---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
---
<Base title="The Engine — DeathOvers"><Navbar />
<main class="analytics-page">
  <section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow"><span></span> THE DEATHOVERS ENGINE</div><h1>CRICKET ISN'T ONE<br /><em>20-OVER STORY.</em></h1><p class="hero-copy">T20, ODI and Test cricket ask different questions. We read every match in its own context: venue, format, innings state and the pressure the game has created.</p><div class="hero-stats"><div><strong>22,479</strong><span>parsed matches</span></div><div><strong>T20 · ODI · TEST</strong><span>format-aware context</span></div><div><strong>5,095</strong><span>successful chases modelled</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="section format-section"><div class="section-label">01 / ONE ENGINE, THREE GAMES</div><h2>THE FORMAT CHANGES<br />THE QUESTION.</h2><div class="format-grid"><article><div class="format-tag">T20</div><h3>IMMEDIATE PRESSURE</h3><p>Every over changes the game. We measure Powerplay intent, middle-over control, death execution and chase targets.</p><span>20 OVERS · PHASE-BY-PHASE</span></article><article><div class="format-tag odi">ODI</div><h3>BUILD, THEN ACCELERATE</h3><p>The same phase logic scales to 50 overs: Powerplay (1–10), Middle (11–40), and Death (41–50), with room for innings-building and late acceleration.</p><span>50 OVERS · PACING MATTERS</span></article><article><div class="format-tag test">TEST</div><h3>THE LONG GAME</h3><p>Tests are not forced into T20 phase labels. We read sessions, innings position, run-rate pressure, wickets in hand and the match situation across days.</p><span>UP TO 5 DAYS · SESSION CONTEXT</span></article></div></section>
  <section class="section intro"><div class="section-label">02 / LIMITED-OVERS PHASES</div><h2>EVERY LIMITED-OVERS<br />INNINGS HAS THREE GAMES.</h2><p>For T20s and ODIs, we split the innings into Powerplay, Middle and Death. The boundaries change by format, but the job of each phase stays clear.</p><div class="phase-grid"><article class="phase-card powerplay"><div class="phase-number">T20 01–06 · ODI 01–10</div><h3>POWERPLAY</h3><p>Field restrictions. Fast starts, new-ball pressure and the first read on the pitch.</p><span>ARE WE SETTING THE TEMPO?</span></article><article class="phase-card middle"><div class="phase-number">T20 07–15 · ODI 11–40</div><h3>MIDDLE</h3><p>Control versus intent. This is where platforms either build or the asking rate starts to bite.</p><span>ARE WE BUILDING ENOUGH?</span></article><article class="phase-card death"><div class="phase-number">T20 16–20 · ODI 41–50</div><h3>DEATH</h3><p>Execution under pressure. Finishers, specialist bowlers and the value of every ball.</p><span>CAN THIS TOTAL BE WON?</span></article></div></section>
  <section class="section split-section"><div><div class="section-label">03 / FIRST INNINGS</div><h2>THE HISTORICAL<br />BENCHMARK.</h2><p>For T20s and ODIs, we compare each phase to previous matches at the same ground and in the same format. In Tests, the equivalent is a session-and-innings baseline—not a fake death-over model.</p><ul class="checks"><li>Venue scoring pattern</li><li>Phase run rate and wickets</li><li>Projected finish using the remaining phases</li></ul></div><div class="scorecard"><div class="card-top"><span>LIMITED-OVERS / EXAMPLE</span><b>VENUE PAR: 172</b></div><div class="phase-row"><span>POWERPLAY</span><strong>46/1</strong><small>PAR 45/1</small><i class="good">+2%</i></div><div class="phase-row"><span>MIDDLE</span><strong>68/3</strong><small>PAR 71/3</small><i>-4%</i></div><div class="phase-row"><span>DEATH</span><strong>58/2</strong><small>PAR 50/2</small><i class="good">+16%</i></div><div class="verdict">PROJECTED FINISH <b>178–186</b></div></div></section>
  <section class="section chase-section"><div class="section-label">04 / THE LIMITED-OVERS CHASE</div><h2>A CHASE NEEDS A<br /><em>DIFFERENT BENCHMARK.</em></h2><p class="wide-copy">This target-adjusted Phase engine is for T20s and ODIs. A 45-run Powerplay means something very different when chasing 130 than when chasing 190. We start with successful chases at this venue, then adjust the target for how the first innings actually played.</p><div class="formula"><span>HISTORICAL PHASE TARGET</span><b>×</b><span>FIRST-INNINGS PITCH SIGNAL</span><b>=</b><strong>LIVE PHASE GOAL</strong></div><div class="chase-example"><div class="chase-head"><span>CHASE TARGET</span><b>186</b><small>Venue: Wankhede · IPL</small></div><div class="target-line"><span>POWERPLAY</span><div class="track"><i style="width: 56%"></i></div><b>56</b><small>historical 52 · adjusted +8%</small></div><div class="target-line"><span>MIDDLE</span><div class="track"><i style="width: 76%"></i></div><b>75</b><small>historical 71 · adjusted +6%</small></div><div class="target-line"><span>DEATH</span><div class="track"><i style="width: 74%"></i></div><b>74</b><small>historical 63 · adjusted +17%</small></div></div></section>
  <section class="section confidence"><div class="section-label">04 / DATA YOU CAN TRUST</div><div class="confidence-grid"><div><h2>WE DON'T PRETEND<br />TO KNOW.</h2><p>Every displayed comparison has a venue sample behind it. When the evidence is too thin, we show less—not more.</p></div><div class="rules"><div><b>✓</b><span><strong>Same venue, same format</strong>We do not mix an ODI ground profile with a T20 benchmark.</span></div><div><b>✓</b><span><strong>Successful chases only</strong>Chase phase targets come from sides that actually reached their target.</span></div><div><b>✓</b><span><strong>Rain-adjusted matches excluded</strong>DLS, VJD and other adjusted results do not enter the model.</span></div><div><b>✓</b><span><strong>Sample size shown</strong>Every target tells you how many comparable chases support it.</span></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="closing"><div class="eyebrow"><span></span> NOT JUST THE SCORE</div><h2>KNOW <em>WHEN</em> THE MATCH<br />IS BEING WON.</h2><a href="/">OPEN LIVE MATCHES →</a></section>
</main></Base>
<style>
.analytics-page{padding:44px 24px 70px;overflow:hidden}.hero{padding:24px 0 54px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.12)}.eyebrow,.section-label{color:var(--bail-amber);font:700 10px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.11em}.eyebrow span{display:inline-block;width:22px;height:2px;background:var(--blood-red);vertical-align:middle;margin:0 8px 2px 0}h1,h2,h3{font-family:'Bebas Neue',sans-serif;font-weight:400;line-height:.94;letter-spacing:.025em}h1{font-size:clamp(56px,10vw,100px);margin:20px 0}h2{font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,64px);margin:14px 0 16px}h3{font-size:27px}em{color:var(--blood-red);font-style:normal}p{color:rgba(240,242,245,.68);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;max-width:620px}.hero-copy{font-size:17px}.hero-stats{display:flex;margin-top:36px}.hero-stats div{padding:0 32px;border-left:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.15)}.hero-stats div:first-child{padding-left:0;border:0}.hero-stats strong{display:block;font:40px 'Bebas Neue';color:#fff}.hero-stats span{font:10px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.48);text-transform:uppercase}.section{padding:66px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.1)}.format-grid,.phase-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}.format-grid article,.phase-card{min-height:250px;padding:22px;background:var(--outfield);border-top:3px solid rgba(240,242,245,.2)}.format-grid article:nth-child(1){border-color:var(--blood-red)}.format-grid article:nth-child(2){border-color:var(--bail-amber)}.format-grid article:nth-child(3){border-color:#7795d3}.format-tag{font:11px 'JetBrains Mono';color:var(--blood-red);margin-bottom:34px}.format-tag.odi{color:var(--bail-amber)}.format-tag.test{color:#9db5eb}.format-grid p,.phase-card p{font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 20px}.format-grid span,.phase-card span{font:9px 'JetBrains Mono';color:var(--bail-amber)}.intro>p{margin-bottom:25px}.powerplay{border-color:var(--bail-amber)}.middle{border-color:#7795d3}.death{border-color:var(--blood-red)}.phase-number{font:11px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.45);margin-bottom:34px}.split-section,.confidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:50px;align-items:center}.checks{list-style:none;margin-top:22px}.checks li{padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.1);font-size:13px}.checks li:before{content:'+';color:var(--blood-red);font-weight:700;margin-right:10px}.scorecard{background:#10131a;border:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.14);padding:19px}.card-top,.phase-row,.verdict{display:flex;align-items:center}.card-top{justify-content:space-between;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.13);font:10px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.55)}.card-top b{color:var(--bail-amber)}.phase-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr .65fr .7fr .4fr;padding:15px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.08);font:12px 'JetBrains Mono'}.phase-row strong{color:#fff}.phase-row small{color:rgba(240,242,245,.48)}.phase-row i{color:#f07c7c;font-style:normal}.phase-row i.good{color:#66d49d}.verdict{justify-content:space-between;padding-top:18px;font:10px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.55)}.verdict b{font-size:20px;color:#fff}.wide-copy{max-width:760px}.formula{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin:30px 0;padding:16px;border:1px dashed rgba(240,242,245,.22);font:10px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.56)}.formula b{color:var(--blood-red);font-size:20px}.formula strong{color:var(--bail-amber)}.chase-example{background:var(--outfield);padding:22px}.chase-head{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;padding-bottom:15px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.1);font:11px 'JetBrains Mono';color:rgba(240,242,245,.55)}.chase-head b{font:35px 'Bebas Neue';color:#fff}.chase-head small{margin-left:auto}.target-line{display:grid;grid-template-columns:110px 1fr 34px 220px;gap:12px;align-items:center;padding:17px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(240,242,245,.06);font:11px 'JetBrains Mono'}.target-line span{color:var(--bail-amber)}.target-line b{font-size:18px;color:#fff}.target-line small{color:rgba(240,242,245,.48)}.track{height:7px;background:#272d37}.track i{display:block;height:100%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--blood-red),var(--bail-amber))}.rules{display:grid;gap:12px}.rules div{display:flex;gap:12px;padding:13px;background:var(--outfield)}.rules b{color:#6ed6a3;font:18px 'JetBrains Mono'}.rules strong{display:block;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:3px}.rules span{font-size:12px;color:rgba(240,242,245,.55);line-height:1.45}.closing{text-align:center;padding:70px 0 15px}.closing h2{font-size:clamp(45px,8vw,76px);margin:18px 0 28px}.closing a{display:inline-block;padding:13px 17px;background:var(--blood-red);color:white;text-decoration:none;font:700 11px 'JetBrains Mono';letter-spacing:.07em}@media(max-width:680px){.analytics-page{padding:30px 16px 50px}.hero-stats{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px}.hero-stats div{padding:0 16px}.hero-stats strong{font-size:31px}.format-grid,.phase-grid,.split-section,.confidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:15px}.section{padding:48px 0}.format-grid article,.phase-card{min-height:0}.formula{display:block;line-height:2}.target-line{grid-template-columns:82px 1fr 28px}.target-line small{grid-column:2/5;font-size:9px}.chase-head small{display:none}.phase-row{grid-template-columns:1.1fr .7fr .8fr .4fr;font-size:10px}}
</style>
